# Component styling

## Long class lists → custom classes

When a JSX element accumulates a long Tailwind class list (layout shell, chrome, multi-state controls), extract a meaningful custom class with `@apply`.

- One CSS file **per section** (e.g. `sidebar/sidebar.css`, `app-layout.css`), colocated with that section.
- Import each file **explicitly** in `src/styles.css` (do not rely on auto-discovery).
- Use `@layer components` and BEM-ish names (`sidebar`, `sidebar__nav`, `sidebar-nav-link`).

```css
@layer components {
  .app-shell {
    @apply flex min-h-dvh bg-background text-foreground;
  }
}
```

**Exception:** Do **not** refactor or wrap styles for Shadcn-generated files under `src/components/ui/`.

## Canonical Tailwind classes

Prefer IntelliSense / Tailwind canonical forms over arbitrary equivalents:

- `rounded-[var(--radius)]` → `rounded-lg` (theme maps `--radius-lg` to `--radius`)
- `outline-none` → `outline-hidden` (Tailwind v4)
- Use `size-*` when width and height match
- Use `gap-*` instead of `space-x-*` / `space-y-*`

Custom utilities that will be used with `@apply` must be registered with `@utility`, not plain `@layer utilities` class selectors.
